  "content": "<p>From UFO-like pileus clouds to ominous shelf clouds, Friday evening’s storms brought a spectacular sky show to the DC area.</p>\n        \n    \n\n      <figure>\n          \n  \n  <img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/size/w30/2026/10/20261016-190549-media1--1-.jpeg\" alt=\"Shelf cloud over the Potomac River Friday evening. \" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n        <figcaption>Shelf cloud over the Potomac River Friday evening. (Ian Elsenbach/CW App)</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n\n  \n\n\n          <p>Published:\n            <time datetime=\"2026-10-16T11:03:09\">Today, 11:03 pm</time>\n          </p>\n    \n    \n      <p>At the end of what may have been the last summerlike day of 2026, the sky put on quite a show. As showers and thunderstorms developed and approached the DC area Friday evening, some remarkable cloud formations appeared overhead.</p><p>First, skywatchers spotted a disc-shaped cloud resembling a UFO. What they were actually seeing was a <em>pileus cloud</em> — a smooth, cap-like cloud that forms above a rapidly growing thunderstorm as rising air cools and moisture condenses.</p><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-76.png\" alt=\"Pileus cloud seen over AU Park in DC Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" /><figcaption>Pileus cloud seen over AU Park in DC Friday evening. (Peter Knudsen/X)</figcaption></figure><p>The pileus cloud formed ahead of the first of two lines of showers and storms that swept through the region between 5 and 9 p.m.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The first line was especially dramatic, preceded by a menacing <em>shelf cloud</em>. This low, horizontal cloud forms along the leading edge of a thunderstorm as cool air rushes outward, often signaling the arrival of strong, gusty winds.</p><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-71.png\" alt=\"Shelf cloud over the Marine Corps War Memorial in Rosslyn, Virginia.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" /><figcaption>Shelf cloud over the Marine Corps War Memorial in Rosslyn, Virginia. (Kevin Ambrose)</figcaption></figure><p>A second line of showers and storms swept through after dark, but by then it was too late to see what other spectacular cloud formations might have been lurking overhead.</p><p>The storms, which fell short of severe limits, formed along a strong cold front which dropped temperatures from highs near 80 late Friday afternoon to lows near 50 Saturday morning.</p><p>Below, find more photos of pileus and shelf clouds shared by our readers.</p><h3>Shelf clouds</h3><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-74.png\" alt=\"Shelf cloud seen from Mount Airy, Maryland Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1814\" /><figcaption>Shelf cloud seen from Mount Airy, Maryland Friday evening. (Scott Jacobson/X)</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-69.png\" alt=\"Shelf cloud over Arlington as storm approaches Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" /><figcaption>Shelf cloud over Arlington as storm approaches Friday evening. (Daniel Blumenthal/CW App)</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-70.png\" alt=\"Shelf cloud over Del Ray Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" /><figcaption>Shelf cloud over Del Ray Friday evening. (Alison Marriott/CW App)</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-78.png\" alt=\"Shelf cloud over DC Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" /><figcaption>Shelf cloud over DC Friday evening. (James Marsh/Facebook)</figcaption></figure><h3>Pileus cloud</h3><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-77.png\" alt=\"Pileus cloud seen over Annandale, Virginia Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"817\" height=\"526\" /><figcaption>Pileus cloud seen over Annandale, Virginia Friday evening. (Jawoo Koo/CW App)</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-73.png\" alt=\"A pileus cloud seen over Arlington Friday evening.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"2667\" /><figcaption>A pileus cloud seen over Arlington Friday evening. (Dimos Katsis/CW App)</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/2026/10/image-75.png\" alt=\"A pileus cloud seen from Alexandria, Virginia Friday evening. \" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" /><figcaption>A pileus cloud seen from Alexandria, Virginia Friday evening. (Geoff Chester)</figcaption></figure><p><em>Kevin Ambrose contributed to this report.</em></p>\n    \n\n          <p>Published:\n            <time datetime=\"2026-10-16T11:03:09\">Today, 11:03 pm</time>\n          </p>\n    \n        \n            <a href=\"https://www.capitalweather.com/author/samenow/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n              <figure>\n                \n  \n  <img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/9b/2a/9b2aed80-72a3-473a-aaf8-035d8a6ee8cb/content/images/size/w30/2026/05/jason_samenow_stylized--4--1-2.png\" alt=\"Jason Samenow\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n              </figure>\n            </a>\n          \n            <h3><a href=\"https://www.capitalweather.com/author/samenow/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Jason Samenow</a></h3>\n\n              <p>Chief meteorologist, journalist, and Capital Weather founder. AMS Certified Digital Meteorologist and DC-area native.</p>\n\n            <p><a href=\"https://www.capitalweather.com/author/samenow/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n              All articles\n              <i>\n  \n</i>            </a>\n          </p>"
